

**What was actually wrong originally:** the merge built a temp file, then pointed `doc_path` *at that temp file* — so "Save" was technically working correctly, just saving to a throwaway path nobody would ever look at again. My fix then made it write directly to the real file immediately, which fixes persistence but breaks discard/undo entirely — exactly what you're now seeing.

**The right fix:** stop treating merge as "build a separate document, then juggle paths." Insert directly into the *currently open* document in memory — same as rotate/delete/move page already do — so it becomes a normal pending change: Save persists it, Save As persists it elsewhere, closing without saving discards it cleanly, no path ever gets touched until the user actually asks.

